  "qualified": [
    "The full web unit/integration and full supervisor unit/integration gates pass with native findings engine floor 3.11.0; the separate company result-only/operational-v2 capability remains reserved for 3.12.0.",
    "Existing result ledger, collection/reduction, private input, source capture, current recipient disclosure, outward history/Inbox/review/webhook/export channels, exact-revision inspection and bounded/concurrent source handling remain covered by the owning T15 checkpoints and full web regression.",
    "Legacy fixture corrections provide real session users and originating runs, preserve negative nonexistent-execution intake, pass current recipients, and observe actual PostgreSQL lock contention rather than SQL spelling. No production source-authorization bypass was added.",
    "Native package lifecycle separates install/trust/explicit enable, including trusted reattachment, and accepts only equivalent absolute-cache/file-URL identities. T16 retains separate actual companion install/contract evidence."
  ],
  "qualificationLimits": [
    "The first full run was interrupted with exit 130 after stale fixture and long recovery failures. Isolated unchanged recovery cases and the final full rerun pass; the earlier timing failure root cause is not asserted.",
    "The next full run passed 5751 checks but one suite failed Docker port binding before tests; cleanup then failed on an uninitialized path. Initializing the owned directory before database startup preserves cleanup, the isolated seven cases pass, and the final full run passes all 5758.",
    "The final web integration run started before the T17 shared ACP delta fix; its owning checks and the subsequent fresh full supervisor suites qualify that seam separately. No exact-build end-to-end package or deployment claim is implied.",
    "Two pre-existing opt-in event-plane load checks are skipped by this default integration lane. This is not their performance qualification.",
    "Actual installed RAH depth-1/depth-2/live access/write-back qualification, CB0 release and all CB1 pilot qualification remain open. No push, merge or deployment occurred.",
    "Brain adds no restrictive source FK or read prerequisite for project deletion; company knowledge remains independent of project lifetime."
  ],
